course: dictionary
lesson: 15362
title: Sooner and soon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sooner means earlier, or in less time than something else. «We will get home sooner by bus than by walking.» The bus takes less time, so it gets you home earlier.
explain: Sooner can also mean «rather». «I'd sooner walk than wait for an hour.» Check it by swapping in «I would prefer to walk»: the sentence still makes sense, so sooner means rather here.
explain: Some phrases use sooner. «The sooner the better» means as early as possible. «Sooner or later» means it will happen at some time. «No sooner had she sat down than the phone rang» means the two things happened almost at once.
fact: Sooner is an adverb. Its family is soon, sooner and soonest.
fact: «Sooner» means earlier, or in less time than something else.
fact: «Sooner» can mean «rather», as in «I'd sooner walk» (I would prefer to walk).
fact: «The sooner the better» means do it as early as possible.
fact: «Sooner or later» means it will happen at some time.
exercise: «Let us leave sooner, before the rain starts.» What does sooner mean here? | Later | Never | *Earlier | Louder
exercise: Sam says, «I'd sooner read than watch TV.» What does sooner mean here? | *Rather | Later | Earlier than the TV | More quietly
exercise: If the bus was due at 9:15 and came 5 minutes sooner, what time did it come? | *9:10 | 9:20 | 10:15 | 9:15
test: Mum says, «The sooner the better» about tidying up. What does she mean? | Never do it | Do it at the very end | *Do it as early as possible | Do it only on Sunday
test: «No sooner had the bell rung than the children ran out.» What does this sentence show? | *Two things happened almost at once | The bell rang many hours later | Nothing happened at all | The children ran out before the bell rang
exam: «We will know the answer sooner or later.» What does sooner or later mean? | *It will happen at some time | It will never happen | It will happen before we ask | It will happen today only
